<title>SRI LANKA: Commercial up on speculation.</title>
<headline>Commercial up on speculation.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Speculation by retail investors that Hatton National Bank Ltd had bid for a major stake in Commercial Bank, drove up the price of Commercial Bank by 4.8 percent, or six rupees to 130, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Small retail investors see the possible link-up as a good move, which can benefit both banks,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>Newspapers reported that Hatton National Bank had made a bid for 40 percent of Commercial Bank, which is held by Standard Chartered Bank.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
